    "sourceId": "why",
    "title": "Why LifeEducation.org Exists",
    "heading": "The Standard",
    "authority": "core",
    "authorityRank": 1,
    "topic": "why",
    "publicUrl": "https://www.lifeeducation.org/why",
    "text": "The Standard\n\nNot what classes they sat through. Not what boxes got checked. Not what looked impressive on paper. What can they actually do, on their own, in real life?\n\nThat is the standard.\n\nTraditional school can help with pieces of that standard. A great school with great teachers can be a powerful environment. I would use one. But school does not deserve automatic trust just because it is official, familiar, compulsory, or credentialed.\n\nToo often school produces compliance without ownership, grades without capability, credentials without judgment, and a habit of waiting to be told what matters. That is not enough."
